  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Direct Assistance to Vulnerable Migrants Transiting through the Northern Parts of the Migration Corridor in Djibouti</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Djibouti has become a transit country in the migration eastern route, hosting complex bi-directional migratory flows. Economic reasons appear to be the main driver for migration (from Ethiopia to the Arab peninsula). Moreover, due to COVID-19, restrictions of movements towards the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia have pushed an increasing number of Ethiopian migrants to return to Ethiopia through Djibouti. The objective of this project is to contribute to reduce vulnerability of migrants transiting through the Republic of Djibouti by providing multisector lifesaving assistance to vulnerable migrants along the migration corridor on the northern parts of the country.</narrative>
  </description>
